    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Bear Empathy",
      "category": "interaction",
      "text": "The werebear can communicate with ursine creatures.\n\n---\n\nThe werecreature can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals of its general kind."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Change Shape",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "concentrate",
        "polymorph",
        "primal"
      ],
      "text": "- Human\n\n- Size Medium\n\n- Melee fist +13 Damage 1d4+7\n\n- Grizzly Bear\n\n- Speed 35 feet\n\n---\n\nThe werecreature changes into its humanoid, hybrid, or animal shape. Each shape has a specific, persistent appearance. A true werecreature's natural form is its hybrid shape.\n\nIn humanoid shape, the werecreature uses its original humanoid size, loses its jaws and claws Strikes, and gains a melee fist Strike that deals bludgeoning damage equal to the slashing damage dealt by its claw.\n\nIn animal shape, its Speed and size change to that of the animal, it gains any special Strike effects of the animal that it didn't already have (such as Grab), and it loses its weapon Strikes.\n\n---",
      "rules": [
        {
          "key": "unsupported",
          "foundry": {
            "alwaysActive": true,
            "key": "RollOption",
            "label": "PF2E.NPCAbility.ChangeShape.Label",
